---
import Layout from "../../layouts/ChinaTravelLayout.astro";

const title = "WeChat Pay Unsupported Card: Fix a Foreign Card That Won't Pay";
const description =
  "Diagnose a WeChat Pay unsupported card: check foreign-card support, verification, QR direction and the fallback order at the counter.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="fixer-page">
    <section class="hero-panel">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker">China Travel Made Easy · Tools</p>
        <h1>WeChat Pay unsupported card: fix a foreign card that won't pay</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Your foreign card is linked, the QR code is right there, and WeChat Pay still refuses
          the payment. Four questions will narrow the cause to a card, verification, flow, or
          limit problem and give you a repair order you can actually use at a counter.
        </p>
        <div class="trust-row" aria-label="Tool properties">
          <span>4 questions</span>
          <span>No sign-up</span>
          <span>No data stored</span>
          <span>Official sources linked</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mono-meta verified-dot">VERIFIED · 17 OCT 2026</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="intro-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
        <h2>Read the message before you blame the card</h2>
        <p>
          A WeChat Pay unsupported card message usually means the card issuer, network, or app
          rules did not accept this particular payment flow. It rarely means the plastic itself
          is broken. That distinction changes what you should try next.
        </p>
        <p>
          This checker takes the symptom you can see — the error, the card, the place — and
          returns the two most likely causes, a short repair sequence, and the backup order to
          use if the queue is moving. It is built for wechat pay travel situations, not for
          account recovery or bank calls.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="seo-section">
      <article class="info-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Symptom one</p>
        <h2>Why a WeChat Pay unsupported card message appears</h2>
        <p>
          When WeChat Pay calls a foreign card unsupported, the card itself is often fine.
          International-card support varies by issuer, country, card network, and the current
          app rules. A Visa or Mastercard that clears a shop counter can still be refused inside
          a restaurant mini program, and the same card can behave differently after a bank
          security review. Treat the message as a signal about the combination of card, account,
          and flow — not as proof that you need a new card.
        </p>
        <p>
          Network choice matters, but no network is a guarantee. Visa and Mastercard are the
          common routes for linking an international card to a payment app; JCB works for some
          issuers; Amex and UnionPay are more often terminal-first and app linking is not
          guaranteed for every card. If your bank or app refuses the link, check the card support
          notice inside WeChat before you assume a specific network is excluded. WeChat Pay for
          tourists is a variable setup, not a single switch.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="info-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Symptom two</p>
        <h2>Verification and payment flow are separate problems</h2>
        <p>
          Real-name verification and card linking are related but not identical. You can have a
          card visible in your wallet and still fail because a passport check, SMS code, or bank
          approval step is unfinished. Conversely, verification can be complete while the card
          issuer blocks the transaction. Finish identity steps before departure, when your home
          phone number and bank app still work — the same steps are much harder from a hotel Wi-Fi
          network at midnight.
        </p>
        <p>
          The flow changes the failure too. Scanning a merchant's QR code, being scanned by the
          cashier, and paying inside a mini program are three different paths. Ride-hailing and
          delivery apps add another merchant account on top. A card that works in one path can
          fail in another, which is why a single test payment at a shop does not prove your setup
          is complete. When you pay with WeChat abroad, match the fix to the flow that failed.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="tool-grid">
      <form class="checker-card" data-wechat-form novalidate>
        <div class="form-header">
          <p class="eyebrow">Symptom check</p>
          <h2>Answer these questions</h2>
          <p>Pick the closest answer. Everything runs in your browser — nothing is sent or stored.</p>
        </div>

        <fieldset>
          <legend>1. Which card are you using?</legend>
          <div class="card-options">
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="visa" required />
              <span>Visa</span>
            </label>
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="mastercard" required />
              <span>Mastercard</span>
            </label>
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="amex" required />
              <span>Amex</span>
            </label>
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="jcb" required />
              <span>JCB</span>
            </label>
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="unionpay" required />
              <span>UnionPay</span>
            </label>
            <label class="option">
              <input type="radio" name="card" value="unsure" required />
              <span>Not sure</span>
            </label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset>
          <legend>2. Is the card linked and verified in WeChat Pay?</legend>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="linked" value="linked" required />
            <span>Yes — linked and verified</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="linked" value="rejected" required />
            <span>No — it was rejected while linking</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="linked" value="not-linked" required />
            <span>Not linked yet</span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset>
          <legend>3. Where does the payment fail?</legend>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="where" value="scan" required />
            <span>I scan the merchant's QR code</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="where" value="scanned" required />
            <span>The merchant scans my payment code</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="where" value="miniapp" required />
            <span>A mini-program checkout or QR menu</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="where" value="app" required />
            <span>A ride-hailing or delivery app</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="where" value="all" required />
            <span>Everywhere I try</span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset>
          <legend>4. What does WeChat show?</legend>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="message" value="unsupported" required />
            <span>Card not supported</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="message" value="identity" required />
            <span>Identity verification needed</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="message" value="limit" required />
            <span>Limit exceeded</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="message" value="bank" required />
            <span>Bank declined the payment</span>
          </label>
          <label class="option">
            <input type="radio" name="message" value="silent" required />
            <span>No message — it just does not succeed</span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <button type="submit" class="button-primary">Diagnose my WeChat Pay failure</button>
      </form>

      <div class="result-card result-placeholder" data-wechat-result aria-live="polite">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your diagnosis</p>
        <h2>Answer the four questions</h2>
        <p>
          The likely causes, the repair order, and your backup payment sequence appear here.
          No account details or card numbers are needed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="seo-section">
      <article class="info-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">After the diagnosis</p>
        <h2>The fallback order when a payment fails at the counter</h2>
        <p>
          At a busy counter, speed beats a perfect fix. Try WeChat Pay once, change the QR
          direction if the cashier can help, then move on: Alipay first, a physical card second,
          and cash last. Alipay and WeChat Pay cover different merchant flows, so a failure in one
          app is not evidence that the other will fail. A physical card still works at hotels,
          airports, and international terminals; cash covers QR-only stalls when both apps and
          cards are blocked.
        </p>
        <p>
          In a mini program, ride-hailing app, or delivery app, confirm the order status before
          you retry or pay a second time. If the flow keeps rejecting your account, ask staff for
          a counter payment or manual ordering path. That is usually faster than proving the app
          should work while other people are waiting.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="info-card caution-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Numbers, not guesses</p>
        <h2>Limits and fees that can look like a card rejection</h2>
        <p>
          Under People's Bank of China guidance, foreign-card payments through Alipay and WeChat
          Pay carry a single-transaction limit of USD 5,000 and a cumulative annual limit of
          USD 50,000. Your bank's daily cap usually binds first. Separately, transactions of
          ¥200 or less are typically fee-free, while larger ones carry a cross-border service fee
          of roughly 3% — a small test payment is therefore a clean way to isolate the problem.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tencent's 2026 promotion waives the 3% international-card fee for 90 consecutive
          calendar days from the first transaction, on daily spending up to RMB 1,000, for
          first-time card linkers. Treat this as a current promotion with conditions, not a
          permanent pricing rule. Confirm current limits, fee notices, and card support on
          official channels inside the app and with your bank before you rely on them.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="explain-grid">
      <article class="info-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">What this tool checks</p>
        <h2>Four inputs, seven causes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Card network</strong> — Visa, Mastercard, Amex, JCB, and UnionPay differ in app-linking support.</li>
          <li><strong>Link status</strong> — a card refused at the link step is a different problem from a payment refusal.</li>
          <li><strong>Failure flow</strong> — scan, be scanned, mini program, and ride-hailing apps take different paths.</li>
          <li><strong>Error text</strong> — "unsupported", "verification", "limit", "bank declined", and no message point to different fixes.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="info-card caution-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Important limitation</p>
        <h2>Diagnosis, not a payment guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          This tool ranks likely causes from the published guidance and the symptoms you select.
          Issuer rules, app versions, and merchant setups change often, and your bank has the
          final word on any transaction. For policy-sensitive decisions, check the
          <a href="/china-travel/sources/">official source library</a> and the notices inside
          WeChat before you travel.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="related-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Related payment guides</p>
      <h2>Read the detail behind each fix</h2>
      <ul class="related-list">
        <li>
          <a href="/china-travel/articles/how-to-use-wechat-pay-in-china-foreigner/">
            <strong>How to Use WeChat Pay in China as a Foreigner</strong>
            <small>Card setup, verification, the 2026 fee waiver, and the fix order at real counters.</small>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/china-travel/articles/wechat-pay-not-working-in-china-foreigners/">
            <strong>WeChat Pay Not Working in China for Foreigners</strong>
            <small>What to try first at a shop counter, a QR menu, or a mini program.</small>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/china-travel/articles/how-to-use-alipay-in-china-foreigner/">
            <strong>How to Use Alipay in China as a Foreigner</strong>
            <small>The first backup route, with its own card-linking and verification steps.</small>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/china-travel/articles/how-to-pay-in-china-tourist/">
            <strong>How to Pay in China as a Tourist</strong>
            <small>The full payment stack, transaction limits, and the backup order when one method fails.</small>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/tools/china-payment-readiness-checker/">
            <strong>China Payment Readiness Self-Check</strong>
            <small>Build the ranked pre-trip payment plan before you need a counter fix.</small>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script type="module" src="/tools/china-wechat-pay-fixer.js"></script>
</Layout>

<style>
  .fixer-page {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .hero-panel {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.8fr) minmax(280px, 0.9fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: stretch;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .intro-card,
  .checker-card,
  .result-card,
  .info-card,
  .related-section {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-media);
  }

  .hero-copy {
    padding: 2.2rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .kicker,
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--seal);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--fs-meta);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.6vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 760px;
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-lede);
  }

  .intro-card {
    padding: 1.4rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .intro-card p {
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  .trust-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .trust-row span {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
  }

  .verified-dot {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--celadon);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
  }

  .seo-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .info-card {
    padding: 1.35rem;
  }

  .info-card p {
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .info-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .info-card ul {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  .info-card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }

  .caution-card {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--paper-dim), var(--surface));
  }

  .tool-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(360px, 0.9fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .form-header {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .form-header p {
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  fieldset {
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  legend {
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  .option {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    transition:
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .option:hover {
    border-color: var(--seal);
  }

  .option:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    background: var(--seal-tint);
  }

  .option input {
    margin: 0;
    accent-color: var(--seal);
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .card-options {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .card-options .option {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .button-primary {
    width: 100%;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--r-none);
    background: var(--seal);
    color: var(--surface);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    min-height: 48px;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .button-primary:hover {
    background: var(--seal-deep);
  }

  .result-card {
    position: sticky;
    top: 5rem;
    padding: 1.35rem;
  }

  .result-placeholder {
    border-style: dashed;
    border-color: var(--hairline);
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  :global(.result-diagnosis) {
    border-color: var(--seal);
  }

  :global(.result-heading) {
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  }

  :global(.result-summary) {
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  :global(.dx-block) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-label) {
    color: var(--celadon);
    font-size: var(--fs-meta);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-list) {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-item) {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-item.is-primary) {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-hard);
  }

  :global(.dx-item-title) {
    color: var(--seal);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-item-detail) {
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  :global(.dx-step) {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  :global(.dx-step-num) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--surface);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    font-size: var(--fs-meta);
  }

  :global(.dx-fallback) {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-fallback-title) {
    display: block;
    color: var(--celadon);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
  }

  :global(.dx-fallback-note) {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-links) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  :global(.dx-links a) {
    display: inline-block;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--celadon);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  :global(.dx-links a:hover) {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    color: var(--seal);
  }

  :global(.dx-note) {
    font-size: var(--fs-meta);
    color: var(--ink-45);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  :global(.button-ghost) {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-none);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    transition:
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  :global(.button-ghost:hover) {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    color: var(--seal);
  }

  .explain-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .related-section {
    padding: 1.35rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .related-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .related-list a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-media);
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    transition:
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .related-list a:hover {
    border-color: var(--seal);
    background: var(--seal-tint);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .related-list strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--celadon);
  }

  .related-list small {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-70);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero-panel,
    .seo-section,
    .tool-grid,
    .explain-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-copy {
      padding: 1.35rem;
    }

    .result-card {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .fixer-page {
      padding: 1.35rem 1rem 3rem;
    }

    .card-options {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
